BaseSettler_recordFillerEscrow
├── when the concrete is PartialFillSettler AND no prior entry exists for the pair
│   └── it should write _fillerRollovers with the supplied srcCstProvided dstCstProduced and destination
├── when the concrete is PartialFillSettler AND no prior entry exists for the pair
│   └── it should increment participantCount by 1 and add dstCstProduced to _totalDstCstEscrowed
├── when the concrete is PartialFillSettler AND a first filler has recorded escrow
│   └── it should leave participantCount at 1 and preserve the first filler's dstCstProduced
│        (genuine multi-filler coverage is owned end-to-end by PartialFillSettler_fill)
├── when the concrete is ExactFillSettler AND _rolloverOutputHash for the orderId is set
│   └── it should write fillRecords at rolloverOutputHash with filler destination dstCstProduced and filledAt of block.timestamp
└── when the concrete is ExactFillSettler AND the same orderId records a second time
    └── it should overwrite the prior fillRecords entry in place because Exact is single-participant
